     <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSH-R1: Number of people benefitting from unconditional and unrestricted cash transfers</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unconditional transfers are provided to beneficiaries without the recipient having to do anything in return in order to receive the assistance . Unrestricted transfers can be used entirely as the recipient chooses i.e. there are no restrictions on how the transfer is spent (Definitions of CALP). It can be delivered e.g. through local banks, shops, traders, local money transfer companies, remittance companies and post offices in either one or several instalments.</narrative>
    </description>
